## 2. Visual reproduction of P0-01 (sidebar controls unreachable)

Manually, in a real browser against `npm run dev`, demo data loaded, wizard
skipped, Timeline page (the demo recording's full 44 events, unvirtualized):

    document.documentElement.scrollHeight  = 1692
    document.documentElement.clientHeight  = 600   (viewport height)
    document.body.scrollHeight             = 1692
    getComputedStyle('.app-shell').overflow = "visible"

1092 of 1692 document pixels (65%) are below the fold. Scrolling to the
bottom of the timeline scrolls the sidebar's own content (which ends at
~320px) completely out of view first - the nav column is blank for most of
the scroll, and every nav item, including the language toggle, is
unreachable without scrolling back to the top. Screenshots:
`docs/evidence/gui-modernization/1.1.0/visual-matrix/phase0-baseline-p0-01-*.png`.

This only reproduces once page content exceeds the viewport - the Overview
page alone (short content) does not trigger it, which is why earlier casual
testing missed it and why the automated test below specifically uses
Timeline, not Overview.

## 3. Automated reproduction (`desktop/tests/visual/shell-layout.spec.ts`)

Playwright, configured to drive the system-installed Chrome
(`channel: "chrome"` in `playwright.config.ts`) rather than a
Playwright-managed download - this build machine's outbound network does not
reach `cdn.playwright.dev` (two attempts, both timed out after 30s), but
Chrome and Edge are both already installed, and Playwright supports driving
either directly. This is recorded as the answer for any future CI runner in
the same position: install `google-chrome-stable` (Linux) or rely on the
OS-bundled Edge (Windows) instead of `playwright install`.

    $ npx playwright test tests/visual/shell-layout.spec.ts --project=chromium --reporter=list

    Running 4 tests using 4 workers
      1) ... sidebar footer stays reachable without scrolling - ar @ min-supported (720x480)
         Expected: <= 480   Received: 1663
      2) ... sidebar footer stays reachable without scrolling - ar @ small (900x600)
         Expected: <= 600   Received: 1663
      3) ... sidebar footer stays reachable without scrolling - en @ min-supported (720x480)
         Expected: <= 480   Received: 1694
      4) ... sidebar footer stays reachable without scrolling - en @ small (900x600)
         Expected: <= 600   Received: 1663
      4 failed

All four fail for the intended reason (the language toggle's bottom edge is
computed at ~1663-1694px regardless of the 480-600px viewport requested),
confirmed by first asserting the reproduction precondition itself
(`document.documentElement.scrollHeight > clientHeight`) is true - a version
of this test that failed because the precondition never held would be a
tautology, not a reproduction, and this run rules that out.

This suite is the Phase 1 acceptance gate: it must pass, unmodified in its
assertions, once ADR 0003 lands.

